<% content_for :title, "Locker wishes" %>

<%# 017 FR-018: Back and Forward must bring back the filter state they left, and
    on this screen Turbo's snapshot cache cannot be trusted to do that. A filter
    change advances the history from inside the frame, and the snapshot for the
    address being left is taken *after* the frame has already been re-drawn — so
    the cache holds, under the old address, markup showing the new filter. Going
    back would replay it and contradict the address bar.

    Opting out means a restoration visit asks the server, which renders whatever
    the address says. It costs a round trip on Back, and buys an address and a
    screen that never disagree. %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <meta name="turbo-cache-control" content="no-cache">
<% end %>

<div class="stack">
  <%= render "locker_wishes/locker_wish_panel" %>
  <%= render "locker_wishes/locker_wish_list" %>
</div>
